  punycode.js 1.2.4, Copyright Mathias Bynens, built into html2canvas
    (licenses/punycode-MIT.txt)
  Pace 1.0.0, Copyright (c) 2013 HubSpot, Inc. (licenses/pace-MIT.txt)

The upstream snapshot also shipped two commercial fonts. Their licences do
not allow redistribution, so in 2026 they were removed from the repository's
current files and from the website:
  Copperplate Gothic Light (src/COPRGTL.ttf): data copyright URW Software &
    Type GmbH, additional data copyright The Font Bureau, Inc., Copyright
    1994 Microsoft Corporation; all rights reserved.
  RocknRoll Typo bold (src/RocknRoll_Typo_bold.ttf): Copyright (c) 2010 by
    Otto Maurer; all rights reserved. The licence embedded in the font says
    it shall not be "made available in any other manner to any third party".
The slideshow now uses these two faces only when a visitor already has them
installed. Fantique Four (assets/site/fonts/Fantique-Four.ttf), by Steve Tune
of Digital Empires (Copyright Digital Empires Inc 1997), is still included:
the licence embedded in the font calls it shareware/donationware and says
"The font is complete as is and you may use it".

Inherited site media are organized under assets/site/, and both versions
of the inherited artwork are preserved under assets/legacy/. Attribution
and license locations are indexed in licenses/README.md; relocation does
not change the rights of the original creators.
